---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { salon } from "../../data/site";

const lastUpdated = "22 August 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Wren Hair Studio collects, uses and protects your personal data, in line with UK GDPR."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-14 sm:pt-20 pb-24">
    <p class="eyebrow text-accent text-xs sm:text-sm mb-4">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display font-black uppercase text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="reveal mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed [&_h2]:font-display [&_h2]:font-black [&_h2]:uppercase [&_h2]:tracked [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_p]:mb-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ul]:space-y-1.5 [&_a]:text-accent [&_a]:underline">
      <div>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {salon.name} ("we", "us", "our") is an independent hair salon
          based at {salon.addressLine1}, {salon.addressLine2}. This policy
          explains how we collect, use and protect personal data when you
          use this website, contact us, or book an appointment, in line with
          the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data
          Protection Act 2018.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or your data can be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${salon.email}`}>{salon.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>What data we collect</h2>
        <p>When you use our contact form or request a booking, we may collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Phone number</li>
          <li>Any message or notes you choose to share with us</li>
          <li>Preferred service, stylist, date and time, for booking requests</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not knowingly collect any special category data (such as
          health information) through this website. If you mention anything
          of that nature in a message to us — for example, a scalp condition
          relevant to a treatment — you do so voluntarily, and we only use
          it to prepare for your appointment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>How we use your data</h2>
        <p>We use the personal data you provide to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to your enquiry or message</li>
          <li>Confirm, manage or reschedule an appointment</li>
          <li>Keep basic client records for returning clients (with your consent)</li>
          <li>Meet our own legal and accounting obligations</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell your data, and we do not use it for automated
          decision-making or profiling.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Legal basis for processing</h2>
        <p>
          We rely on your <strong>consent</strong> (given via the checkbox on
          our contact and booking forms) to process the details you submit
          through this website, and on our <strong>legitimate interest</strong>{" "}
          in running the studio to keep basic appointment records for
          existing clients. You can withdraw consent at any time by
          contacting us — see "Your rights" below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>How long we keep your data</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiry and booking request details are kept for up to 12 months,
          or for as long as you remain an active client, whichever is
          longer. After that, we delete or anonymise the data unless we're
          required to keep it for a longer period by law (for example, basic
          financial records).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Who we share your data with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not share your personal data with third parties for
          marketing purposes. We may share limited data with trusted service
          providers who help us run the studio and this website — for
          example, our website hosting provider (Netlify) and, if you book
          through it, our online booking provider. These providers only
          process data on our instructions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not use tracking or advertising cookies of its
          own. Any cookies set directly by us are strictly necessary for the
          site to function (for example, remembering that you've submitted a
          form).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ask what personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>Ask us to correct inaccurate data</li>
          <li>Ask us to delete your data</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
          <li>Object to how we process your data</li>
          <li>Complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) if you believe we've mishandled your data</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${salon.email}`}>{salon.email}</a>. You can find
          out more about your rights and how to complain at{" "}
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top
          of this page shows when it was last revised.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
